      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While relying solely on visual cues or speech patterns to judge a guest's risk or disposable income can be subjective and potentially discriminatory, it is vital that your manual emphasizes objective behavioral indicators such as public intoxication, aggression, excessive volume, or attempts to make a scene. Staff should be trained to prioritize guests based on documented VIP status or specific security alerts rather than making snap judgments based on appearance or dress code to avoid liability and maintain consistency. By focusing on observable behaviors like unlogged group arrivals or attempts to bypass entry protocols, your team can ensure safety without stereotyping.",
